#X obj 675 8 flow.sync;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 240 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 the object stores the last received value from each
inlet and \, when a new value arrives \, outputs all stored values
from all outlets from rightmost to leftmost;
#X text 240 138 unlike [flow.sync_pack] \, which packs all hot inlets
into a single list on one outlet \, [flow.sync] keeps a separate stored
value for each inlet and outputs all of them in parallel from N outlets
on every new input;
#X text 240 208 all inlets are hot \, so any float \, symbol or list
triggers the output;
#X text 240 248 the object can be used to synchronize parallel control
streams \, for example to output several parameter values together
when any of them changes;
